},"terrain":{"product":"LOLA_LDEM_80S_20M","post_m":20.0,"vertical_error_m":2.0},"note":"Clear: the terrain stays below the line between the antennas by more than the terrain map\u2019s height error; blocked: it rises above by more than that; uncertain: the map cannot tell. The radio path is clear only if the space around the line of sight that the radio signal needs is clear too. Ground within two map cells of either end is not counted as a blocker. The finest available terrain covering the lander's ground and the whole requested neighbourhood is used. A gap at the lander or a window edge can require a coarser model; gaps along a ray remain uncertain."},"meta":{"computed_at":"2026-10-02T20:49:48.216944Z","uncertainty":{"kind":"composite","parts":[{"source":"Terrain height (lunar terrain map)","note":"A cell is uncertain when the map\u2019s height error (2 m for cells 20 m wide) could tip it either way; the shares are ranges for that reason."},{"source":"Antennas and radio","note":"Antenna heights and the frequency are assumed unless given; the line of sight depends on the heights, the radio path also on the frequency."}]},"engines":{"los":"los-3"},"sources":[{"name":"Lunar terrain map (LOLA_LDEM_80S_20M)","url":"https://pds-geosciences.wustl.edu/lro/lro-l-lola-3-rdr-v1/","issued_at":null,"fetched_at":null,"licence":null,"snapshot_id":null}],"stale":false,"compute_ms":34.762457999022445}}